## Issues

- [ ] `src/service/install/index.ts` — `configureVscode` is never imported or
  called from the orchestrator. `configureZed` is called (line 122) and its
  result assembled into `steps[]` (line 135), but `configureVscode` from the
  same `configureIde/index.ts` module has no call site anywhere in `src/`. The
  assembled `steps[]` (lines 125-137) therefore never includes a VS Code IDE
  step. The spec requires IDE configuration to present both Zed and VS Code
  options as an inherent decision; `applySteps` already has branch logic for VS
  Code `instructions` steps, confirming the step type is load-bearing. A
  consumer calling `aide_init` with `category: "ide"` receives no VS Code step.
  Traces to: `src/service/install/.aide` outcomes.desired ("IDE configuration
  is presented as optional — the consumer asks whether the user wants Zed and/or
  VS Code configuration, and only applies what they confirm.") and outcomes.desired
  ("IDE steps that require external tooling (e.g., VS Code extension install via
  CLI) return instructions for the consumer to execute.").
  Misalignment: implementation-drift
  Deferred to kanban: [[configurevscode-is-dead-code-never-called-from-install-orche]]

## Retro

Items 1 (stale comment) and 3 (JSDoc lie about brainPath) were resolved cleanly
by targeted edits. The configureVscode gap remains the single outstanding drift
item and is being tracked exclusively in kanban — no further action required in
this todo until the kanban task is actioned.
